  "id": "DrugBank_DB14031 - MONDO_20541",
  "verbalization": "Tretamine appears to be associated with the treatment of Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary through a series of indication links, suggesting a potential therapeutic relationship. The evidence is supported by the presence of Tretamine in the indication of Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary and Belotecan, both of which are linked to the same target condition. This indicates that Tretamine may have a role in the treatment of this tumor type, possibly through mechanisms that are not yet fully understood. The shared pathway involves Melphalan and Belotecan, which are known to target germ cell tumors, suggesting a possible overlap in their biological effects. The integration of these indications supports the hypothesis that Tretamine could be a candidate for repurposing in the treatment of Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary, though further mechanistic investigation is required to confirm the exact mode of action.",
